      "side": 1,
      "message": "It was mostly to have a symmetry with `unshare` which receives `paddr`, converts it to `vaddr` and copies _from_ it, while `share` would return `paddr`, converted from the `vaddr` it copied _to_.\n\nI agree that it\u0027s better to give a meaningful name to a variable rather than \"`vaddr`\" (all dereferenceable variables are VAs, after all) and would be happy to rename both to `copy`. Although I\u0027d rather use the term \"bounce buffer\" (\"`bounce`\") to clarify the reason for which we\u0027re copying it; WDYT?",
